  "answer": "This has been requested before. The team tracks it under the epic terminal#11111 (Admin-specific customizations). One of that epic's user stories is \"I want to use a different `profile.defaults` block when running elevated\". Related requests are terminal#3246 (different color scheme when running as Administrator) and terminal#14593 (different appearance when running as Administrator). terminal#14593 was closed as a duplicate of #3246 and #8311. It isn't implemented yet. The team is holding off because of the combinatorial explosion of appearance states (focused/unfocused × elevated/unelevated, and so on). The epic floats ideas such as `profiles.elevatedDefaults`, a separate `admin-settings.json`, or a `showWhenElevated` option, but none is committed. The tickets don't offer a built-in workaround. For now, subscribe to terminal#11111 and add your use case there, including the `sudo` `disableInput` scenario. You can also keep a dedicated elevated profile with its own color scheme, as you already do. Another option is to make the shell prompt or tab title show when it's elevated, a workaround suggested in terminal#1939."
